\subsection{Learning results}

We plot the mean change of $p^{\mathrm{\sss TV}}$ and $p^{\mathrm{\sss TV}}$ throughout the EM iteration in Figure \ref{fig:p-diff}. The difference in $p^{\mathrm{\sss TV}}$ and $p^{\mathrm{\sss TV}}$ reached the threshold of $\epsilon = 0.01$ in the 15-th iteration. Thus, the convergence of the EM algorithm is confirmed. 

Compared with the ground truth data in the test set, 78.8\% and 78.5\% of our predictions on longitudinal decisions of LV and TV were in line. Note that the prediction task in this paper is a real-time decision prediction on vehicle longitudinal maneuvers. Related research \cite{rahmati2021helping} achieves an accuracy of 82.1\% for a simultaneous game on behavior-level decisions, that is, turning or waiting. In this context, the prediction accuracy of the proposed model is satisfactory for longitudinal decision-making modeling.

