We also compare against three existing attacks for ViM: Lee \textit{et al.} \cite{abs-2408-11679}, BadScan \cite{BadScan_abs-2411-17283} and QRDBA \cite{QRDBA_NagaonkarTM25} by using a 10\% poisoning rate.
It demonstrates that the proposed BadViM can achieves higher attack success rate than all three existing attacks.
