\item $\mathcal{M}$ and $\mathcal{N}$ have two inner tangent points iff the roots of $f(\lambda) = 0$ are $-a^2$,$-a^2$,$-\delta^2/a^2$ where $a^2<\delta$.
 \item  $\mathcal{M}$ and $\mathcal{N}$ have only an intersection point and an inner tangent point iff $f(\lambda) = 0$ has a triple root, less than $-a^2$.%  \textcolor{blue}{and $a^2<\delta$ , CREO QUE ESTA CONDICI\'ON AUNQUE SE DE, SOBRA. SI HAY RAIZ TRIPLE MENOR QUE $-a^2$, ENTONCES SE TIENE $a^2<\delta$} 
