Going the other way, suppose that $f(\lambda) = 0$ has a triple root, less than $-a^2$. Obviously that implies that $r_1=r_2=r_3, r_1<-a^2$, such that each solution of this system gives rise to two different points of intersection, one of multiplicity three and the other of multiplicity one. 

Namely, the set of solutions of the system of equations $r_1=r_2=r_3$ with $r_1<-a^2$ is described  as follows, %in terms of the variable $x_3$ as follows, 
\begin{eqnarray*} 
 t_1 = t_3, & t_2 = t_3,& t_3  \neq 0,\quad t_3^2  \neq 1,\\  
