From the coefficients of the polynomials $g(\lambda)$ and $q(\lambda)$, we can deduce the following observations.

\begin{enumerate}
\item  Since $b^2+a^2>0$,  $-a^2$ is a root of $f(\lambda)$ iff  $x_c= 0$; besides if $x_c\neq 0$, $g(\lambda)$ must have a negative root, that is, $f(\lambda)$ must have a negative root less than $-a^2$.

\item $f(\lambda)=-\dfrac{( \lambda+a^2 )( \lambda+b\delta )^2 }{a^2b^2}$ iff  $x_c= 0$ and $|y_c|=b+\delta$.

\item  Since $b^2+a^2>0$, $b^2$ is a root of $f(\lambda)$ iff  $y_c= 0$; besides if $y_c\neq 0$, $q(\lambda)$ must have a negative root, that is, $f(\lambda)$ must have a root less than $b^2$.
\end{enumerate}

