	be the height of the point of the lower path $P$
	%and upper path $Q$, respectively, 
	lying at abscissa $I$. Then we have the convergence in law
	\begin{align}\label{eq:limitlawLow}
		\frac{P_n(I)}{n^{3/4}} \longrightarrow \frac{1}{3}Z.
	%,
	%$$
	%when $n$ goes to infinity. Here the random variable $Z$ is equal to 
	%$$
	\end{align}
	when $n$ goes to infinity, where $Z$ is an in Theorem~\ref{thm:tamari}. Again, we have the convergence of all moments.
