\section{CPU Time Analysis}
Figure \ref{fig:cputime} shows that generated BO algorithms
run in the same ballpark as \emph{TuRBO1}
($\sim\!0.3$ s on an M1 Pro), and an order of magnitude faster than \textsc{HEBO}.
Note that LLAMBO’s required CPU time as reported by the authors are $3$s (on their hardware) and LLAMBO also requires either a payed LLM API or significant GPU hardware.

