Indeed, \cref{th:semilattice+dualdiscr} indicates that \emph{any} degree \( d \) \sos\ proof of $p\geq 0$, for any polynomial $p$, can be computed in \( n^{O(d)} \) time with arbitrary precision (not only degree-$d$ $\sos$ proofs for $-1\geq 0$, as required by refutation). %Furthermore, our proof will show (\cref{sect:applications}) that \(\sos\) resolves the refutation problem in polynomial time, thus ensuring polynomial bit complexity (refer to the discussion immediately preceding \cref{sect:contribution}).

