\begin{abstract}
We establish an assume-guarantee (AG) framework for compositional reasoning about multi-objective queries in parametric probabilistic automata (pPA)\textemdash{}an extension to probabilistic automata (PA), where transition probabilities are functions over a finite set of parameters. 
We lift an existing framework for PA to the pPA setting, incorporating asymmetric, circular, and interleaving proof rules. 
Our approach enables the verification of a broad spectrum of multi-objective queries for pPA, encompassing probabilistic properties and (parametric) expected total rewards. 
Additionally, we introduce a rule for reasoning about monotonicity in composed pPAs.
\end{abstract}

