The results were compared, identifying three types of dependencies in grouping the criteria sets. All methods indicated agreement on the role of the environmental criteria (C1-C4), with average weights of approximately 0.07 and minimal standard deviations. This consistency is more noticeable, as shown by the compact boxplots and closely spaced scatter plot markers for these criteria in Fig.~\ref{fig:weight_distribution}, indicating agreement among the methods concerning the significance of environmental criteria in the sustainability evaluation process.

\begin{figure}[htbp]
