To obtain edit mechanisms under incomparable observations, we introduce the property of $ic$-enforceability that characterizes whether an edit function has the ability to enforce opacity under the incomparable observation setting.
Specifically, we construct an edit mechanism in a two-player game scheme with imperfect information between the system and the edit function.
In the end, we show that the edit function is $ic$-enforcing if it can be  synthesized from the edit mechanism. 
