    By taking advantage of the constructions of $\mathbf{O}_I$ and $\mathbf{O}_D$, if the system generates an event unobserved by the intruder (the edit function), the intruder is assumed to ``observe'' (the edit function is assumed to ``react'', i.e., output the same event) via self-loops in the corresponding states.
    Also, one can notice that the estimate of the intruder is not necessarily the same as the estimate of the edit function since their observations are incomparable.

