\section{Related Work}

% DDI Prediction Datasets
\paragraph{DDI Prediction Datasets}
Numerous datasets have been developed for DDI prediction, varying in scope and annotation strategies. 
DrugBank~\cite{wishart2018drugbank} is the most comprehensive and widely used.
However, its DDI information is presented as free-text descriptions rather than structured labels or relations.
% DrugBank~\cite{wishart2018drugbank} is the most comprehensive and widely used, but its DDI information is presented as free-text descriptions rather than structured relations.  
% Moreover, the associated metadata of drugs is not systematically organized into distinct modalities, limiting its direct applicability for multimodal machine learning models.
The associated drug metadata is also not systematically organized into distinct modalities, limiting its applicability for multimodal machine learning.
Several DDI-focused datasets have been constructed based on DrugBank and supplementary sources such as FAERS~\cite{faers2024}, MEDLINE~\cite{medline2024}, and other biomedical databases. 
These datasets are typically single-modal, providing DDI information using either text or SMILES strings. 
