Among them, some describe interactions without assigning labels (e.g., LIDDI~\cite{banda2015provenance}, TDC~\cite{huang2021therapeutics}, BioSNAP~\cite{biosnapnets}),
while others provide binary or inconsistently defined label sets without a systematic scheme, and often omit relation directionality (e.g., SemEval 2013~\cite{bjorne2013uturku}, HODDI~\cite{wang2025hoddi}, TWOSIDES~\cite{tatonetti2012data}, Mendeley DDI dataset~\cite{yu2020data}).

The DDInter dataset~\cite{xiong2022ddinter} represents a recent state-of-the-art with emphasis on multimodality.
