\paragraph{Data preprocessing}

The data for the experiment come in two forms: spectrograms (Figure \ref{fig:default_normal}), as well as mel scale spectrograms (mel spectrograms) (Figure \ref{fig:default_mel}). Both were obtained using the Librosa Python library. The first is a visual representation of signal frequencies over time, while the latter is a spectrogram specially adjusted to the Mel scale, which is a perceptual scale adjusted to human hearing ~\cite{mel_spectrogram}.

