\noindent\textbf{Document-wide context is essential.} As seen in \autoref{table:results}, methods leveraging contextual information widely outperform non-contextual methods across \emph{ConTEB} tasks. These results highlight the critical role of context-aware embeddings in improving retrieval performance in such settings, whether through untrained late chunking approaches or expensive context-aware reformulation approaches.
As expected, the gap is even more notable in \emph{ConTEB}'s controlled setting experiments. 


